<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="ranged.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="ranged">
    <!-- target_ui::run → the w_target targeting side panel. Slice 2a: the host
         builds draw_ui_window's shallow sections (title / cursor / gun+recoil or
         spell / target info / turret list / controls) into one colour-tagged
         `body_rml` string via target_ui::panel_text(), run through cata_text_to_rml
         (\n → <br/>). The aim / hit-chance readout is a WIP stub here (slice 2b).
         Render-only: the keyboard aim/fire loop is unchanged; the map aim overlay
         stays on the sprite path. -->
    <div class="panel ranged-panel">
        <div class="ranged-body scroll-pane">
            <div class="ranged-text" data-rml="body_rml"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
